  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nNot much change in the forecast this period. We are currently still \ncaught between two ridges with moisture and mid-level energy \nbringing some convection toward the coast during the daytime. Today \nlooks a little less conducive for a continued active sea-breeze, but \nmodels are suggesting scattered showers/storms along the coast in \nthe morning and into the afternoon, especially for the northern \nCoastal Bend has energy rotates northward around the eastern ridge. \n\nSeasonal temperatures are expected with a very slight uptick toward \nthe second half of the week. Highs will be above 100 daily over the \nRio Grande Plains and in the 90s east. Heat index values increase \nfor the latter half of the period and heat advisories may become \nnecessary by mid-week.",
